[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. The reports in it say three. Each now has
a ticket of its own, with the reports it covers.

## Where each one stands

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October.

- **`parser`**: fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`). Ticket closed.
- **`hint`**: won't fix. The `booking-v3` form is retired, so no new reports can come through it.
  Ticket closed as not planned.
- **`shift`**: still open. Neither change touches it.

<Callout kind="warn">
Closing #4471 did not close every problem in it. Expect more <code>shift</code> reports, and file
them on its own ticket, not on #4471.
</Callout>

## What the reports show

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

- **`parser`**: the tenant writes the day first and the shared parser reads the month first.
  The booked date and the invite date are the same two numbers, flipped (7 April becomes 4 July).
- **`hint`**: a report that came in through the `booking-v3` form at a day-first tenant. That form
  prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so people type the month first and the form reads it
  the tenant's way. Same symptom, different code: the fix is the form's hint, not the parser.
- **`shift`**: the date moves by one day, not by a month (Tuesday 12 May becomes Monday 11 May; a
  client in Lisbon gets Tuesday, one in Toronto gets Monday). A time zone bug. The desk read these
  as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`). As the desk counts, they stay in the `parser` count where
  they are filed by tenant, and the `shift` row lists them again.

## Why it looked like one

- Dedupe matches on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  "Wrong day on the invite" reads the same for all three problems, so all three were merged.
- The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. A US browser got tagged `hint` whatever
  form it used; a local browser on the `booking-v3` form got tagged `parser`. Compare the
  "intake tagged" column above: the tag does not tell the problems apart. Tenant, form and
  channel do (`causes.ts`).
- Each export row counts once by id. The export pages overlap, so some reports appear twice.

